  "2026-10-02T17:08:45.621Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-10-02: complete strict all-status corpus read returned 2851/2851 items with no omissions or unreadable files; exact GitHub issue/ID and contract-title searches found no canonical owner for this residual acceptance. Existing foundations are linked, including closed historical work; no closed fix is asserted outstanding. Imported report and acceptance are planning evidence, not current reproduction or implementation completion. This item remains open and unclaimed until selected for implementation."
body: "## Outcome and ownership\nChild of #1357. Add a shared knowledge lifecycle for observations, assertions and decisions so agents can distinguish what was observed, what is asserted, and what is currently authoritative for a task.\n\nReuse existing custom item fields, evidence references, immutable history, typed relationships and supersedes. #656 already implements a temporal digital-twin exemplar and event-time replay; this proposal promotes reusable knowledge-reconciliation semantics rather than rebuilding that package. This is planned scope, not a claim that every primitive is absent.\n\n## Implementation plan\n1. Inventory current schema, provenance, evidence and temporal APIs. Define a versioned SDK contract with stable knowledge identity, record kind, subject/predicate or typed payload, source/evidence references, author provenance, recorded time, observed time, validity interval and verification state. Treat unknown values explicitly.\n2. Implement a pure reducer over immutable records for current/as-of knowledge. Retain alternatives and conflict sets; classify corroboration, correction, explicit supersession, expiration and unresolved contradiction. Domain policy may resolve a conflict only with a recorded reason and evidence. Newer timestamp alone must not establish truth.\n3. Bind verification to the exact evidence/source revision and validity policy. Changed or expired evidence invalidates the verification result without erasing historical proof. Prevent cycles or ambiguous supersession from silently selecting a winner.\n4. Reuse the relationship graph for downstream dependencies. Compute bounded invalidation sets for compiled context, decisions and checkpoints affected by a change; expose fingerprints and continuation receipts.\n5. Add thin CLI/MCP views and mutation adapters, generated contracts, migration documentation and SDK examples. Legacy prose remains readable and explicitly untyped/unverified unless a deliberate migration supplies evidence.\n\nIllustrative names only: KnowledgeRecord, reconcileKnowledge, KnowledgeConflict, KnowledgeInvalidationReceipt. Select final names after inventory.\n\n## Acceptance and tests\n- [ ] Same event set and declared policy yields deterministic current/as-of results, including late and out-of-order observations\n- [ ] Conflicting assertions are surfaced with both evidence paths; no silent last-writer-wins truth\n- [ ] Superseding a decision preserves its historical validity and invalidates exactly the affected downstream dependencies\n- [ ] Verification of evidence revision A cannot validate changed revision B; expiration requires refresh or explicit abstention\n- [ ] Historical reads preserve recorded-time versus valid-time distinctions and report unknown/ambiguous intervals\n- [ ] Tests cover correction, retraction, overlap, missing evidence, deleted source, cycle, duplicate delivery, concurrent append and clock-skew inputs\n- [ ] Property tests verify replay determinism and invalidation convergence; packed SDK consumer and CLI/MCP parity prove the public boundary\n- [ ] Bounded results expose omitted work and continuation; small-workspace cost and current quality gates do not regress\n\n## Dependencies\nFeeds the semantic-coverage, checkpoint and scenario workstreams in #1357. Contract design can proceed in parallel with policy separation. Reuse the existing context engine and evidence lineage rather than creating a second source of truth.\n\n## Non-goals\nNo universal automated fact checker, model-generated confidence treated as verification, arbitrary rewrite of immutable history, new domain-specific ontology imposed on every project, or automatic resolution based only on popularity/recency.\n\n## Linked implementation slices\n- Supplies knowledge validity/conflict semantics to #1361 and dependency validation to #1359\n- Reuses policy separation from #1360\n- Decision scenarios and negative controls: #1362"
